  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Alive, not Dead",
      "type": "trait",
      "_id": "adeptusActor09It",
      "img": "modules/impmal-core/assets/icons/blank.webp",
      "system": {
        "notes": {
          "player": "",
          "gm": "<p>When the Chastener makes an attack on an enemy and the damage results in their death with a weapon with the Inflict (Stunned) or (Restrained) traits, they may instead choose for the target to become Unconscious. The Chastener also gains +1 SL on Presence (Intimidation) and Intuition tests during an interrogation.  Arbitrator Commander: As an Action, the Arbitrator may make a Presence (Leadership) Test. For every SL, a single Enforcer that can hear the Arbitrator may take an Action.   Call for Backup: As an Action, an Arbitrator can call for backup. This call is heard by all Enforcers in a 1-mile radius. Backup usually arrives in 1d10 Rounds (or minutes if out of combat) but may be shorter or longer depending on distance.   Guilty until Proven Innocent: As an Action, the Arbitrator can make an opposed Presence (Intuition) vs Discipline (Composure) Test to unearth guilt or evidence of a crime, reducing the party's Superiority by 1 if successful.</p>"
        },
